## =========================================================================
## flyscan configuration template
##
## Same syntax as a pscan .con file, so pscan's own actions work here. Unlike
## pscan, position in the file does NOT decide when a block runs: anything
## before 'action apt_fly' is setup, anything after it is teardown. There is
## no per-coordinate pipeline for a block to fall into.
##
## Run with:  flyscan --dry-run example_flyscan.con
## =========================================================================

## -------------------------------------------------------------------------
## SETUP - runs once, before anything moves
## -------------------------------------------------------------------------
action script
script echo "fly scan starting"
end

## -------------------------------------------------------------------------
## FOCUS
##
## Over a field wider than ~100 um, sample tilt alone usually exceeds the
## depth of focus (roughly lambda / 2*NA^2 - about 310 nm at 400 nm, NA 0.8),
## and signal strength follows focus quality. So focus is measured at a grid
## of points before the scan, fitted to a surface, and then applied once per
## line - which is all the Phidget analog output needs to keep up with.
##
## coarse <start_um> <stop_um> <step_um>   the first, wide sweep
## fine_span / fine_step                   optional second pass about the peak
## grid <nx> <ny>                          focus measurement points
## surface  plane | quadratic              plane needs 3 points, quadratic 6
## metric   copeak | dc                    what counts as "in focus"
## every_lines <n>                         re-measure during the scan; 0 = never
## -------------------------------------------------------------------------
action autofocus
coarse 0 100 10
fine_span 10
fine_step 1
grid 3 3
surface plane
metric copeak
every_lines 20
limits 0 100
end

## -------------------------------------------------------------------------
## FAST AXIS - swept at constant velocity, one ASOPS sweep per pixel
##
## VELOCITY IS THE DIAL. One ASOPS sweep covers velocity/sweep_rate, and that
## is the native sample spacing; how many fit in the line is the scope's
## segment count. There is no 'pixels' key - specifying both would
## over-determine it.
##
## scan <start_mm> <stop_mm>    two values, not three
## velocity <mm_per_s>          the one knob that sets sampling and time
## bin <nm>                     OUTPUT pixel size, for post-processing only.
##                              Averages bin/native_pitch copeaks together,
##                              for sqrt(that) times the SNR.
## runup <mm>                   constant-velocity lead-in, outside the scan
## acceleration <mm_per_s2>     optional, to check the run-up is long enough
## spot <um>                    optical resolution, for the smear check
## limits <min_mm> <max_mm>     must cover the travel INCLUDING the run-up
## unidirectional               bare flag; omit for a bidirectional raster
##
## At 10 kHz, 5 mm/s gives 0.5 um per sweep - half a 1 um spot, which is the
## ceiling. Above it each copeak smears over more than half a resolution
## element and binning cannot recover it. The MLSA02 would do 250 mm/s; at
## 5 mm/s you are using 2% of it.
## -------------------------------------------------------------------------
action apt_fly
axis 0
scan 53.500 53.600
velocity 5.0
bin 1000
runup 0.050
acceleration 9810
spot 1.0
limits 53.400 53.700
end

## -------------------------------------------------------------------------
## SLOW AXIS - an ordinary pscan apt_stage block, stepped once per line
## -------------------------------------------------------------------------
action apt_stage
axis 1
scan 37.000 37.100 0.001
limits 36.900 37.200
end

## -------------------------------------------------------------------------
## SCOPE - one Sequence-mode acquisition per line
##
## channels / roles / sparsing correspond one to one.
##   ac       the Brillouin signal, kept at full rate
##   dc       probe DC, denominator of dR/R - one value per copeak
##   trigger  BBD303 position-trigger pulses; measured position beats inferred
##   spare    anything else
##
## Sparsing the trigger channel is bounded by the TTL pulse WIDTH: sparse
## harder than the pulse is wide and pulses are missed entirely.
##
## segment_window is how much of each 12.5 ns delay window to keep, in lab
## seconds. Half the window is 50 us, which at 10 MS/s is 500 points.
## -------------------------------------------------------------------------
action scope_line
ip 192.168.74.2
channels C1, C2, C3
roles ac, dc, trigger
sparsing 1, 100, 20
sample_rate 10000000
segment_window 50e-6
sweep_rate 10000
transfer_rate 4.0
end

## -------------------------------------------------------------------------
## TEARDOWN - runs once, after the scan
## -------------------------------------------------------------------------
action script
script echo "fly scan finished"
end
